5.\tab Creating P?S/8 output files from the contents of paper-tapes.\par
\par
In this operating mode, the contents of paper-tapes will be processed into the contents of P?S/8 output files.  There are two variants to this operating mode:\par
\par
a)\tab Output is created as a collection of up to 17 TFS output files.  \tab Sufficent files must be passed to avoid error messages indicating \tab data overflow.  The count of output files created will be \tab available in the final program summary.  Unused files are ignored \tab and can be repurposed.  This output mode is used when the '/E' \tab command-line option switch is not set.\par
\par
b)\tab Output is created as a collection of up to eight extended-length \tab output files.  [Note: Smaller P?S/8 configurations may only \tab support fewer than eight logical device units limiting the \tab maximum output size.  Additionally, the amount of space available \tab to an extended-length file is subject to several configuration \tab issues including the underlying size of the storage device.]  \tab This output mode is used when the '/E' command-line option switch \tab is set.\par
\par
Specific command-line options that apply are as follows:\par
\par
\tab /E\tab This command-line option switch determines the output mode \tab\tab\tab as defined above.\par
\par
\tab /S\tab This command-line option switch suppresses all console \tab\tab\tab output with the exception of error messages as described \tab\tab\tab above.  [This is known as silent-running mode.]\par
\par
\tab /U\tab This command-line option switch determines the exact \tab\tab\tab\tab character set of all console messages as described above.\par
\par
\tab /V\tab This command-line option switch enables verbose message mode \tab\tab as described above.  This option is ignored if the '/S' \tab\tab\tab [silent running mode] is enabled.\par
